@Override
public int getMaxAggregatedValueByteSize() {
  if (_nominalEntries == 0) {
    return 8;
  }
  if (_nominalEntries == 1) {
    return 16;
  }
  int longSizeInBytes = Long.BYTES;
  int intSizeInBytes = Integer.BYTES;
  return (_nominalEntries * (longSizeInBytes + intSizeInBytes)) + 24;
}
```

## How the Max Byte Size Is Computed

- If `_nominalEntries` is 0, it returns 8.
- If `_nominalEntries` is 1, it returns 16.
- Otherwise, it multiplies `_nominalEntries` by the combined size of one long plus one int (`Long.BYTES + Integer.BYTES`), then adds 24.

The accompanying documentation notes this represents the maximum storage assuming the worst case, described as the sketch being in `"estimation mode, which requires storing theta and count."`

